  "explicit_limitations": [
    "This is an immutable hardening layer over BRD-044, not a replacement or mutation of the accepted BRD-044 evidence.",
    "This artifact compares linear-elastic 2D implementations sharing idealized geometry, sections, loads and boundary conditions; agreement cannot validate omitted physics.",
    "This is not F2 or L2: no 3D grillage, shell or solid model, moving-load analysis, mesh convergence, bearing-foundation-soil interaction or bridge-code load combination is present.",
    "No strength, serviceability, stability, fatigue, robustness, durability, construction-stage or hazard capacity is calculated; no safe, feasible, verified, design-pass or utilization verdict is permitted.",
    "The backend identity is pinned to one Python executable and OpenSees binary. Trust remains bounded by the operator-selected executable and site-packages directory, whose bytes are recorded and checked but whose publisher authenticity is not established here.",
    "site-packages is appended after existing interpreter paths. Any bridge_evolution module loaded in the worker is a structured failure; no fallback to frame_f1 is permitted.",
    "The absolute-plus-relative tolerances are deterministic code-verification tolerances, not acceptance limits from a bridge design standard.",
    "G2 and G4 are not passed: model-quality and independent-design gates require a real bridge design basis, higher-fidelity model, blind reproduction and discrepancy reconciliation."
  ]
}
